    },
    "body": "The native geometric reader lacked learned multi-token span composition. This change gives original token rows shared signed-2I actions, predicts HOLD/OPEN/APPEND/COMMIT, and supplies the committed ordered product to the existing reader. Four q/k maps remain absent; old-held timing, separate validity, exact occurrence identity and save/load bindings are retained.\n\nThe fixed two-seed authored common-endpoint task completed 320 updates each. Original answers are 99/128 and 128/128; head-zero source majorities are 128/128 and 127/128. LastToken reduces these to 27 answers/41 sources and 44 answers/44 sources, supporting accumulated composition's contribution. Both reload and post-ablation restoration are exact. The report preserves seed one's answer-path errors, full causal interventions and all artifact identities.\n\nExecuted source is `cfdf535a800e343873699ca4693f7b11f9a2e32d`, with the exact retained executable. Delivery separately integrates current main's prime-pointer route from #1587. This is a mixed float offline component, not natural-language qualification, matched algebra superiority or full integer serving. The roadmap advances exact token-action/register export and preserves offline donor weight recompilation.\n\nValidation: 35 focused checks and the example build passed at executed source; 19 combined-source compatibility checks passed. Fit plus evaluation took 1,368.529 seconds with maximum RSS 131,301,376 bytes. No extra seed/dose/selector sweep or paid compute.\n\nReferences #1512 and #973.\n",
